NOTE: this is Leon's fork of grate-driver/xf86-video-opentegra, used for
Surface RT (Tegra 3) graphics bring-up on postmarketOS. His work is on the
dri3-present branch: DRI3 screen support, Present support (copy mode), Present
page-flip (check_flip/flip/unflip), and a fix to drm_tegra_bo_from_dmabuf
(initialise the bo list heads, drop the lseek size probe that dma-bufs reject).
DRI3 and Present worked on hardware, but this fork is no longer developed: the
OpenRT project dropped this DDX in favour of the generic modesetting driver with
glamor and Wayland, and the device now runs modesetting. Tooling and write-up:
https://github.com/LBSiUK/SurfaceRT-GPU-Driver

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

xf86-video-tegra
Open-source X.org graphics driver for NVIDIA Tegra

All questions regarding this software should be directed at the
Xorg mailing list:

        http://lists.freedesktop.org/mailman/listinfo/xorg

Please submit bug reports to the Xorg bugzilla:

        https://github.com/grate-driver/xf86-video-opentegra/issues

The master development code repository can be found at:

        https://github.com/grate-driver/xf86-video-opentegra
